# adocs/data/S148_rfp_ceiling_sweep.py --mined, run at 192a5a3 on the machine
# .moltke.local.md describes, 2026-09-08, against the tune build. The table
# S148 chooses its challenger from.
#
# WHAT IS NEW HERE. Every earlier reading of this axis is six values wide --
# S145's [0, 3, 6, 10, 15, 63] over the 48 rows the constructed set held then,
# S154's re-take of the same six at `fc5526e`. The set is 82 rows since S168
# and the ceiling had never been swept over them. S148's challenger rule names
# one integer:
#
#   C1 = the largest ceiling at which both the mate in four and the mate in
#        five exact counts over the 82 rows are non-zero
#
# which is a statement about every value from 0 to 15. This is that table, and
# it reads C1 = 4.
#
# WHAT IT SAYS.
#
#   the mate in five class is the binding one: 11, 9, 6, 4, 1 exact of 16 at
#   ceilings 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, and 0 from 5 up. The mate in four class survives
#   further -- 13, 14, 10, 10, 7, 4, 5, 3, 2, 2 through ceiling 9 -- and is
#   still 1 of 16 at the shipping 15, which is where the S145-era claim of
#   "0 of 8" now reads on the larger set.
#
#   the curve is flat from 10 up: exact 39/82, m3 12/24, m4 1/16, m5 0/16 at
#   every value from 10 to 15. "10 is already indistinguishable from 63" holds
#   on this grid too, one value lower than S145 and S154 could see.
#
#   the whole-set count moves 39 -> 52 of 82 between 15 and 4, the mate in
#   three class 12 -> 18 of 24, and the mined breadth set 145 -> 159 exact of
#   318. `short` and `sign` are 0 at every one of the sixteen settings, which
#   is the defect column and is what makes the rest a strength reading.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. Nothing here is Elo. The ceiling is what confines the
# pruning to the nodes nearest the leaves, so a lower one searches more nodes
# per iteration and reaches fewer plies under a clock; S085's SPSA run moved
# this axis the other way and the vector that held 15 was verified at +21.02.
# The trade is the SPRT of adocs/data/S148_sprt.sh and not this table.
#
# `RfpMinPly` is held at 3 throughout, read from the binary rather than
# written down: floor and ceiling are one guard read two ways and S145
# measured them substituting for each other, so a sweep that moves both
# attributes nothing (S145's own header).
#
# The script imports S145_rfp_sweep and calls its sweep(); this directory is
# append-only, so adocs/data/S145_rfp_sweep.log is left as it was taken and
# the re-run lands here.

